1. MISSION

Implement a fully operational, reusable Academic Administration module within the existing Curriculum Server architecture.

The objective is to establish the academic administration environment that every successfully provisioned school instance can use independently.

The module must allow an authorized school administrator to:

1. Configure the school's academic sessions.
2. Configure academic terms and calendars.
3. Create and manage classes.
4. Create and manage class arms or streams.
5. Register and manage subjects.
6. Register and manage teachers.
7. Register and manage students.
8. Assign teachers to subjects and classes.
9. Enrol students into classes and academic sessions.
10. Maintain student academic progression and class history.
11. Manage academic relationships and assignments.
12. Configure the academic structure required by subsequent examination modules.

This must be a real, persistent, tenant-isolated implementation.

Do not deliver another demonstration module, mock academic dashboard, seeded operational school, fabricated student records, simulated teacher registrations or local JSON-based substitute for production persistence.

The module must be reusable across all future provisioned school instances.

It must not require a separate codebase or separate deployment for every school.

It must support different institutional structures, education systems, academic calendars and grading configurations.

Important: Phase 2 establishes the academic administration foundation. It does not implement the examination engine or the complete assessment and results system.

Do not implement Phase 3, Phase 4 or Phase 5 features as part of this assignment.

